7.inferred-typing
Inferred typing means TypeScript automatically determines the type from the value, so we don't need to explicitly write the type.
example:

let name = "Vignesh";
let age = 28;
let isActive = true;

name     → string
age      → number
isActive → boolean

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.Explicit vs inferred
“Type inference means TypeScript automatically identifies the type of a variable based on the value assigned to it, so we don't always need to explicitly specify the type.”
 example:
 Explicit typing:

let name: string = "Vignesh";

Inferred typing:

let name = "Vignesh";

In both cases, TypeScript knows name is a string.

