9.array
An array in TypeScript is used to store multiple values. We can specify the type of elements the array should contain, such as string[], number[], or Employee[], which provides type safety.”
example:
let skills: string[] = ["JavaScript", "Node.js", "TypeScript"];

skills.push("React"); // ✅

skills.push(100);     // ❌ Error

