10.duck typing
“Duck typing means TypeScript checks an object's structure. If the object has the required properties and methods with compatible types, TypeScript accepts it regardless of its actual type or class name.”
example:
interface User {
    name: string;
    age: number;
}

const employee = {
    name: "Vignesh",
    age: 28,
    salary: 50000
};

function printUser(user: User) {
    console.log(user.name);
}

printUser(employee); // ✅ Works

