14.Default Parameter in TypeScript
“A default parameter is a function parameter that has a predefined value. If the caller doesn't provide that argument, the default value is automatically used.”
example 
function concatStrings(
    str1: string,
    str2: string,
    str3: string = "hi"
): string {
    return str1 + str2 + str3;
}
