16.What is a class in TypeScript?
A class in TypeScript is a blueprint for creating objects. It contains properties and methods and supports object-oriented concepts like encapsulation, inheritance, abstraction, and polymorphism.
example:
class BankAccount {
    public name: string;
    private balance: number;

    constructor(name: string, balance: number) {
        this.name = name;
        this.balance = balance;
    }

    getBalance(): number {
        return this.balance;
    }
}

const account = new BankAccount("Vignesh", 10000);

console.log(account.name);         // ✅
console.log(account.getBalance()); // ✅
console.log(account.balance);      // ❌ private

